G3D: System as upstream G3D 8.x declares and initialises it (g3d SVN r30 G3D.lib/include/G3D/System.h,
source/System.cpp), plus upstream's RegistryUtil (r30 include/G3D/RegistryUtil.h, source/RegistryUtil.cpp,
unmodified), which the 2016 fork dropped. PLAYER evidence:
  - System is 0x20 bytes larger: the ctor 0x009d7570 default-constructs a std::string at +0x34 between
    m_numCores (+0x30) and m_machineEndian (+0x50): upstream's m_appDataDir (0x1c bytes, and the 8-byte
    aligned LARGE_INTEGER m_start/m_counterFrequency then move 4 more). m_version is at +0xa0, init
    stores m_highestCPUIDFunction at +0xc8 (ours +0xa8).
  - System::init 0x009d7030 reads the CPU speed from the registry: it builds std::strings from
    "HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\HARDWARE\DESCRIPTION\System\CentralProcessor\0" (0x00bbd328) and "~MHz"
    (0x00bbd36c) and calls RegistryUtil::readInt32 0x009e5d40 with &m_cpuSpeed (+4); the fork stores 999.
  - RegistryUtil::readInt32 0x009e5d40 and the static getRootKeyFromString 0x009e5c70 are byte-identical
    to r30's RegistryUtil.cpp compiled with the G3D flags.
  - initTime 0x009d6cf0, getStandardProcessorExtensions 0x009d6f60, init and System() become identical
    (LARGE_INTEGER members and QueryPerformance* calls as upstream).

